{"id":"mahabharata-3-268","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":268,"title":"अष्टषष्ट्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 268 · Angada's embassy and the siege","summary":{"en":"Angada delivers Rama's challenge in Ravana's court, shakes off the Rakshasas who seize him, and leaps back over the city. The monkeys then storm Lanka, breaking its walls and gates, before withdrawing at Rama's command.","kn":"ಅಂಗದನು ರಾವಣನ ಸಭೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಶ್ರೀರಾಮನ ಸವಾಲನ್ನು ತಿಳಿಸಿ, ಹಿಡಿಯಲು ಬಂದ ರಾಕ್ಷಸರನ್ನು ಕೊಡವಿ ನಗರದ ಮೇಲೆ ಹಾರಿ ಮರಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅನಂತರ ಕಪಿಗಳು ಲಂಕೆಯ ಮೇಲೆರಗಿ ಗೋಡೆ ಬಾಗಿಲುಗಳನ್ನು ಮುರಿದು, ಶ್ರೀರಾಮನ ಆಜ್ಞೆಯಂತೆ ಹಿಂದಿರುಗುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"अङ्गद रावण की सभा में श्रीराम की चुनौती सुनाते हैं, उन्हें पकड़ने वाले राक्षसों को झटक देते हैं और नगर के ऊपर से कूदकर लौट आते हैं। फिर वानर लंका पर धावा बोलकर उसकी दीवारें और द्वार तोड़ते हैं, और श्रीराम के आदेश पर लौट आते हैं।","te":"అంగదుడు రావణుని సభలో శ్రీరాముని సవాలును వినిపించి, పట్టుకోవడానికి వచ్చిన రాక్షసులను విదిలించి నగరం మీదుగా దూకి తిరిగివస్తాడు. తర్వాత వానరులు లంకపై దాడి చేసి గోడలు, ద్వారాలు ధ్వంసం చేసి, శ్రీరాముని ఆజ్ఞతో వెనక్కి వస్తారు.","ta":"அங்கதன் ராவணனின் சபையில் ஸ்ரீராமரின் அறைகூவலை அறிவித்து, தன்னைப் பிடிக்க வந்த அரக்கர்களை உதறி நகரின் மேல் தாவித் திரும்புகிறான். பின்னர் வானரங்கள் லங்கையைத் தாக்கி அதன் மதில்களையும் வாயில்களையும் உடைத்து, ஸ்ரீராமரின் ஆணைப்படி பின்வாங்குகின்றன.","ml":"അംഗദൻ രാവണന്റെ സദസ്സിൽ രാമന്റെ വെല്ലുവിളി അറിയിക്കുന്നു; അദ്ദേഹത്തെ പിടികൂടുന്ന രാക്ഷസന്മാരെ അദ്ദേഹം കുടഞ്ഞെറിയുന്നു, നഗരത്തിനുമീതെ ചാടി മടങ്ങുന്നു. പിന്നെ കുരങ്ങന്മാർ ലങ്കയെ ആക്രമിച്ച്, മതിലുകളും കവാടങ്ങളും തകർക്കുന്നു; രാമന്റെ കൽപ്പനപ്രകാരം അവർ പിന്മാറുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.268; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"द्रौपदीहरणपर्व","titleEn":"Draupadiharana Parva (Abduction of Draupadi)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"प्रभूतान्नोदके तस्मिन्बहुमूलफले वने ।\nसेनां निवेश्य काकुत्स्थो विधिवत्पर्यरक्षत ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that forest, rich in food, water, roots, and fruit, Rama camped the army and guarded it according to the rules."}},{"n":2,"text":"रावणश्च विधिं चक्रे लङ्कायां शास्त्रनिर्मितम् ।\nप्रकृत्यैव दुराधर्षा दृढप्राकारतोरणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ravana too arranged Lanka's defenses as the treatises prescribe, a city already hard to assault, with firm ramparts and gates."}},{"n":3,"text":"अगाधतोयाः परिखा मीननक्रसमाकुलाः ।\nबभूवुः सप्त दुर्धर्षाः खादिरैः शङ्कुभिश्चिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seven moats of unfathomable water, teeming with fish and crocodiles, were made unassailable, studded with stakes of khadira wood."}},{"n":4,"text":"कर्णाट्टयन्त्रदुर्धर्षा बभूवुः सहुडोपलाः ।\nसाशीविषघटायोधाः ससर्जरसपांसवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The ramparts were made formidable with ear-shaped turrets and engines, with battering rams and stones, with jars of venomous snakes for fighters, and with powdered resin."}},{"n":5,"text":"मुसलालातनाराचतोमरासिपरश्वधैः ।\nअन्विताश्च शतघ्नीभिः समधूच्छिष्टमुद्गराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were equipped with pestles, firebrands, iron arrows, spears, swords, axes, and the shataghni, with maces smeared in wax."}},{"n":6,"text":"पुरद्वारेषु सर्वेषु गुल्माः स्थावरजङ्गमाः ।\nबभूवुः पत्तिबहुलाः प्रभूतगजवाजिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At all the city gates stood troops, fixed and moving, with many foot soldiers and abundant elephants and horses."}},{"n":7,"text":"अङ्गदस्त्वथ लङ्काया द्वारदेशमुपागतः ।\nविदितो राक्षसेन्द्रस्य प्रविवेश गतव्यथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Angada reached the gate of Lanka, was announced to the rakshasa king, and entered without fear."}},{"n":8,"text":"मध्ये राक्षसकोटीनां बह्वीनां सुमहाबलः ।\nशुशुभे मेघमालाभिरादित्य इव संवृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the midst of many crores of rakshasas the very powerful Angada shone like the sun ringed by clouds."}},{"n":9,"text":"स समासाद्य पौलस्त्यममात्यैरभिसंवृतम् ।\nरामसंदेशमामन्त्र्य वाग्मी वक्तुं प्रचक्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Ravana, who was surrounded by ministers, the eloquent Angada announced Rama's message and began to speak."}},{"n":10,"text":"आह त्वां राघवो राजन्कोसलेन्द्रो महायशाः ।\nप्राप्तकालमिदं वाक्यं तदादत्स्व कुरुष्व च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Rama of Kosala, of great fame, says to you, king: here are words fitting the time; take them up and act."}},{"n":11,"text":"अकृतात्मानमासाद्य राजानमनये रतम् ।\nविनश्यन्त्यनयाविष्टा देशाश्च नगराणि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a king without self-control gives himself to wrongdoing, lands and cities caught in that wrong are destroyed."}},{"n":12,"text":"त्वयैकेनापराद्धं मे सीतामाहरता बलात् ।\nवधायानपराद्धानामन्येषां तद्भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"You alone wronged me, by taking Sita by force; for that, others who have done no wrong will be killed."}},{"n":13,"text":"ये त्वया बलदर्पाभ्यामाविष्टेन वनेचराः ।\nऋषयो हिंसिताः पूर्वं देवाश्चाप्यवमानिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The forest-dwelling sages you harmed before, in your pride of strength, the gods you insulted,"}},{"n":14,"text":"राजर्षयश्च निहता रुदन्त्यश्चाहृताः स्त्रियः ।\nतदिदं समनुप्राप्तं फलं तस्यानयस्य ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"the royal sages you killed, the women you seized and made weep, all this is the fruit of your wrongdoing that has now come."}},{"n":15,"text":"हन्तास्मि त्वां सहामात्यं युध्यस्व पुरुषो भव ।\nपश्य मे धनुषो वीर्यं मानुषस्य निशाचर ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will kill you with your ministers. Fight, be a man. Night-wanderer, see the strength of the bow of a mere human."}},{"n":16,"text":"मुच्यतां जानकी सीता न मे मोक्ष्यसि कर्हिचित् ।\nअराक्षसमिमं लोकं कर्तास्मि निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Release Sita, Janaka's daughter; you will never escape me. With sharp arrows I will make this world free of rakshasas.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"इति तस्य ब्रुवाणस्य दूतस्य परुषं वचः ।\nश्रुत्वा न ममृषे राजा रावणः क्रोधमूर्छितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the envoy spoke these harsh words, King Ravana, dizzy with rage, could not bear them."}},{"n":18,"text":"इङ्गितज्ञास्ततो भर्तुश्चत्वारो रजनीचराः ।\nचतुर्ष्वङ्गेषु जगृहुः शार्दूलमिव पक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Understanding their master's signal, four night-wanderers seized Angada by his four limbs, as birds seize a tiger."}},{"n":19,"text":"तांस्तथाङ्गेषु संसक्तानङ्गदो रजनीचरान् ।\nआदायैव खमुत्पत्य प्रासादतलमाविशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Carrying those night-wanderers clinging to him, Angada leapt into the sky and landed on the roof of the palace."}},{"n":20,"text":"वेगेनोत्पततस्तस्य पेतुस्ते रजनीचराः ।\nभुवि संभिन्नहृदयाः प्रहारपरिपीडिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he sprang up with speed, those night-wanderers fell to the ground, their hearts broken and bodies crushed by the blows."}},{"n":21,"text":"स मुक्तो हर्म्यशिखरात्तस्मात्पुनरवापतत् ।\nलङ्घयित्वा पुरीं लङ्कां स्वबलस्य समीपतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Released from the palace summit, he again sprang across the city of Lanka and landed near his own army."}},{"n":22,"text":"कोसलेन्द्रमथाभ्येत्य सर्वमावेद्य चाङ्गदः ।\nविशश्राम स तेजस्वी राघवेणाभिनन्दितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Angada went to the king of Kosala, reported everything, and, praised by Rama, the glorious one rested."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततः सर्वाभिसारेण हरीणां वातरंहसाम् ।\nभेदयामास लङ्कायाः प्राकारं रघुनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Rama, delight of the Raghus, with the full onrush of the monkeys, swift as the wind, broke Lanka's rampart."}},{"n":24,"text":"विभीषणर्क्षाधिपती पुरस्कृत्याथ लक्ष्मणः ।\nदक्षिणं नगरद्वारमवामृद्नाद्दुरासदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lakshmana, with Vibhishana and the king of the bears in front, crushed the difficult southern gate of the city."}},{"n":25,"text":"करभारुणगात्राणां हरीणां युद्धशालिनाम् ।\nकोटीशतसहस्रेण लङ्कामभ्यपतत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A hundred thousand crores of monkeys, strong in battle, with limbs the color of young camels, fell upon Lanka then."}},{"n":26,"text":"उत्पतद्भिः पतद्भिश्च निपतद्भिश्च वानरैः ।\nनादृश्यत तदा सूर्यो रजसा नाशितप्रभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As monkeys leapt, fell, and plunged, the sun, its light dimmed by dust, could not be seen."}},{"n":27,"text":"शालिप्रसूनसदृशैः शिरीषकुसुमप्रभैः ।\nतरुणादित्यसदृशैः शरगौरैश्च वानरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Monkeys like rice blossoms, like shirisha flowers, like the young sun, and like golden arrows"}},{"n":28,"text":"प्राकारं ददृशुस्ते तु समन्तात्कपिलीकृतम् ।\nराक्षसा विस्मिता राजन्सस्त्रीवृद्धाः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"saw the rampart all around turned tawny with them, and the rakshasas, including women and the old, were amazed all around, king."}},{"n":29,"text":"बिभिदुस्ते मणिस्तम्भान्कर्णाट्टशिखराणि च ।\nभग्नोन्मथितवेगानि यन्त्राणि च विचिक्षिपुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They broke jeweled pillars and turret tops, and flung away the engines, broken and ripped from their moorings."}},{"n":30,"text":"परिगृह्य शतघ्नीश्च सचक्राः सहुडोपलाः ।\nचिक्षिपुर्भुजवेगेन लङ्कामध्ये महाबलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking up shataghnis with wheels, rams, and stones, the mighty ones hurled them with the force of their arms into the middle of Lanka."}},{"n":31,"text":"प्राकारस्थाश्च ये केचिन्निशाचरगणास्तदा ।\nप्रदुद्रुवुस्ते शतशः कपिभिः समभिद्रुताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever hosts of night-wanderers stood on the ramparts then fled by hundreds, pursued by the monkeys."}},{"n":32,"text":"ततस्तु राजवचनाद्राक्षसाः कामरूपिणः ।\nनिर्ययुर्विकृताकाराः सहस्रशतसंघशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then at the king's command, rakshasas who could take any form came out in hundreds of thousands, in horrible shapes,"}},{"n":33,"text":"शस्त्रवर्षाणि वर्षन्तो द्रावयन्तो वनौकसः ।\nप्राकारं शोधयन्तस्ते परं विक्रममास्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"raining weapons, driving off the forest-dwellers, and, cleaning the rampart, they showed great valor."}},{"n":34,"text":"स माषराशिसदृशैर्बभूव क्षणदाचरैः ।\nकृतो निर्वानरो भूयः प्राकारो भीमदर्शनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Terrible to see, the night-wanderers, dark as heaps of black gram, again cleared the rampart of monkeys."}},{"n":35,"text":"पेतुः शूलविभिन्नाङ्गा बहवो वानरर्षभाः ।\nस्तम्भतोरणभग्नाश्च पेतुस्तत्र निशाचराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many bulls among monkeys fell with their limbs split by spears, and many night-wanderers fell, broken by pillars and gate arches."}},{"n":36,"text":"केशाकेश्यभवद्युद्धं रक्षसां वानरैः सह ।\nनखैर्दन्तैश्च वीराणां खादतां वै परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rakshasas and monkeys fought hair against hair, tooth and nail, heroes biting one another."}},{"n":37,"text":"निष्टनन्तो ह्युभयतस्तत्र वानरराक्षसाः ।\nहता निपतिता भूमौ न मुञ्चन्ति परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Monkeys and rakshasas on both sides groaned; the slain, fallen to the ground, still would not let go of each other."}},{"n":38,"text":"रामस्तु शरजालानि ववर्ष जलदो यथा ।\nतानि लङ्कां समासाद्य जघ्नुस्तान्रजनीचरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama rained showers of arrows like a cloud, and they reached Lanka and killed the night-wanderers."}},{"n":39,"text":"सौमित्रिरपि नाराचैर्दृढधन्वा जितक्लमः ।\nआदिश्यादिश्य दुर्गस्थान्पातयामास राक्षसान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lakshmana, son of Sumitra, with his firm bow and tireless, pointed out the rakshasas in their fortifications one by one and brought them down with iron arrows."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततः प्रत्यवहारोऽभूत्सैन्यानां राघवाज्ञया ।\nकृते विमर्दे लङ्कायां लब्धलक्षो जयोत्तरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, at Rama's order, the armies withdrew, for the havoc in Lanka had achieved its aim and victory was theirs."}}]}]}